==Strategy==
The optimal way to beat the stage is to rush down the base using [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] with research combos and a defense combo. If Ramen Cat is Lv.40 with a defense combo, Ramen will survive 7 hits from the Dragons, though it will still survive 6 hits at Lv.37 even without the combo. Simply spam Ramen initially without leveling wallet, then add Courier after the first doge spawns, then at 75% of the way to across the map, launch Bahamut as the 2nd dragon spawns to shove both of them behind the base and destroy it.

An alternate strategy is to attempt to deal with the Li'l King Dragons while they come out, however if allowed to stack up, defeating them may become impossible. They have a limited supply, so defeating even a few early on can be a great help in this stage but this is not recommended if rushing is an option.

You can also bring any other [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rusher]]-class units at your disposal, as they can serve as a secondary  Awakened Bahamut Cat, allowing you to deal more damage then you would be able to with just one A. Bahamut. [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]] is the only viable crowd-controller, as unlike other [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|Anti-Traitless]] crowd-controllers, Supercat does not desync the Li'l King Dragons.  Courier Cat is a great help in this stage, as he is able to quickly deal damage to the Li'l King Dragons and can deal heavy damage to the peons in this stage.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] - A very good option for this stage as he is a spammable, high health meatshield who can tank many hits from the Li'l King Dragons as well as the peons.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - A very good option here as he has good base damage and helps chip down the Li'l King Dragon Cat and manages the peons with good enough meatshielding.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - Can be used to burst down a large portion of the Li'l King Dragon's HP, provided you can keep the peons in check.

